From: Aurélien Pommel <aurelien.pommel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: core: shorten the tuning block's data timeout

The spec's 150 ms bounds 40 tuning commands, not each one. A sample phase on
the edge of the card's window can miss the data start bit, and the read then
waits out the timeout: on dw_mmc at 150 MHz the controller's maximum, 112 ms,
on one boot in three to one in two. 15 ms keeps four times the per-command
budget.

---
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/mmc_ops.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/mmc_ops.c
@@ -710,9 +710,11 @@
 	/*
 	 * According to the tuning specs, Tuning process
 	 * is normally shorter 40 executions of CMD19,
-	 * and timeout value should be shorter than 150 ms
+	 * and timeout value should be shorter than 150 ms.
+	 * That is the whole process: a phase that loses the
+	 * data start bit must not wait out the full 150 ms.
 	 */
-	data.timeout_ns = 150 * NSEC_PER_MSEC;
+	data.timeout_ns = 15 * NSEC_PER_MSEC;
 
 	data.sg = &sg;
 	data.sg_len = 1;
